      "user_input": "(discord_avatar_url or RpgClubUserAvatarHistory.where(:user_id => params[:user_id]).where.not(:avatar_url => ([nil, \"\"])).order(:changed_at => :desc, :event_id => :desc).pick(:avatar_url))",
      "confidence": "Weak",
      "cwe_id": [
        601
      ],
      "note": "False positive. The target is not request input. It is either the Discord CDN URL discord_avatar_url builds from the member's stored discord_avatar hash (only built when the hash matches Discord's /\\A(a_)?\\h{32}\\z/ shape and the user id is all digits), or the stored avatar_url from avatar history, which only the bot's service token can write (UserAvatarHistoryController#create requires require_service!). params[:user_id] only picks the row. The action also redirects only when trusted_image_url? passes (https on cdn.discordapp.com, media.discordapp.net, *.backblazeb2.com or the BACKBLAZE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL host) and streams the blob otherwise. Brakeman cannot see that guard. Covered by the 'never redirects off the trusted image hosts' and 'ignores a Discord avatar hash that isn't one Discord issues' specs."
    }
